# packages/images/agent/container-hardening.env — the canonical
# container-hardening contract for the blitzlog-agent container.
#
# Issue #164 ("harden the agent container — non-root, dropped
# capabilities, read-only rootfs").
#
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the hardening flags that
# every `docker run` of the agent image must carry. It is consumed by:
#
#   * the host-side watchdog
#     (infra/aws/packer/scripts-docker-ubuntu/watchdog.sh), which is
#     baked into the EC2 AMI as /usr/local/bin/container-hardening.env
#     by the Packer `file` provisioner + the `cp` in 02-systemd.sh;
#   * the local dev tasks in mise.toml (`mise run image-*`), which
#     source it straight out of the repo.
#
# It is a POSIX `KEY=value` file with NO code — no arrays, no bashisms —
# so it can be sourced by `sh` (dash) as well as `bash`. Every value
# uses `:=` so an operator can override it from the environment.
#
# tests/test_container_hardening.py asserts that:
#   * the flags below are carried by EVERY `docker run` site (the
#     watchdog + all five mise dev tasks);
#   * the writable-path list matches the table in docs/DOCKER.md;
#   * the uid/gid/home below agree with the Dockerfile.
#
# The list cannot silently grow: adding a writable path here without
# documenting it in docs/DOCKER.md fails the test suite.

# --- Identity of the unprivileged container user -----------------------
# The image creates a `blitzlog` user/group with these ids and a
# `USER blitzlog` directive. The host-side watchdog chowns the bind
# mounts it exposes to the container to this uid/gid, because a bind
# mount preserves the SOURCE's ownership — a root-owned 0700 directory
# is unreadable to the container's non-root user.
: "${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_UID:=1000}"
: "${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_GID:=1000}"

# The agent's HOME inside the container. Relocated away from /root when
# the container stopped running as uid 0.
: "${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_HOME:=/home/blitzlog}"

# --- Tier 1: inert hardening flags -------------------------------------
# Applied to every `docker run` of the agent image.
#
#   --security-opt=no-new-privileges:true  blocks setuid elevation, so
#                                           third-party npm code that
#                                           runs in-container cannot
#                                           gain privileges.
#   --cap-drop=ALL                         drops Docker's default
#                                           capability set (CAP_NET_RAW,
#                                           CAP_SYS_CHROOT,
#                                           CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE,
#                                           CAP_MKNOD, CAP_SETUID,
#                                           CAP_SETGID). The base agent
#                                           path needs none of them.
#   --pids-limit                           bounds the process count so
#                                           a fork bomb cannot exhaust
#                                           the host's PIDs.
#   --init                                 runs docker-init as PID 1 so
#                                           orphaned grandchildren are
#                                           reaped instead of piling up
#                                           as zombies for the life of
#                                           the run.
#   --read-only                            makes the container's rootfs
#                                           read-only, so the agent
#                                           cannot rewrite the binaries
#                                           it runs (/usr/local/bin/
#                                           {opencode,git,gh,
#                                           whisper-cli}) and serve the
#                                           tampered copy for the rest
#                                           of the session.
: "${BLITZLOG_PIDS_LIMIT:=1024}"
BLITZLOG_HARDENING_FLAGS="--security-opt=no-new-privileges:true --cap-drop=ALL --pids-limit=${BLITZLOG_PIDS_LIMIT} --init --read-only"

# --- The writable-path contract -----------------------------------------
# With --read-only, every path the agent legitimately writes to has to
# be carved out explicitly. A --read-only rootfs with an implicit hole
# is worse than no flag at all, so this list is:
#
#   1. explicit — it is the complete set, not a sample;
#   2. documented — the table in docs/DOCKER.md mirrors it verbatim;
#   3. asserted — tests/test_container_hardening.py fails if the two
#      drift apart, so the list cannot silently grow.
#
# `/home/blitzlog` is a tmpfs because it is the agent's HOME: the global
# git config ($HOME/.gitconfig), mise's toolchain ($HOME/.local), the
# npm/npx cache ($HOME/.npm), opencode's own state ($HOME/.local/share,
# $HOME/.cache) and the opencode + telegram-bot config dirs
# ($HOME/.config) all live under it. The tmpfs is owned by the
# container's unprivileged uid, so the agent can write its own HOME and
# nothing else. ($HOME/.config additionally carries a nested tmpfs —
# see BLITZLOG_TMPFS_MOUNTS below for why.)
#
# `/tmp` is a tmpfs for scratch space (pip/npm/node temporaries).
#
# `/var/log/blitzlog` and `/workspace` are bind mounts from the host —
# they are writable because the agent must write logs (the host uploads
# them to S3) and must clone/edit/commit/push the repository. The host
# chowns both to the container's uid.
BLITZLOG_WRITABLE_PATHS="/tmp ${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_HOME} /var/log/blitzlog /workspace"

# The tmpfs mounts that back the writable paths above. Stored as
# ready-to-splat flag strings.
#
# `$HOME/.config` gets its OWN tmpfs, nested inside the `$HOME` one.
# It looks redundant — it is inside a writable path already — but it is
# load-bearing:
#
# Docker creates the MISSING PARENT of a bind mount as `root:root 0755`.
# The gh CLI config is bind-mounted at `$HOME/.config/gh`, so Docker
# creates `$HOME/.config` itself — and it lands INSIDE the `$HOME`
# tmpfs, owned by root. The agent runs as uid 1000 and can therefore
# not create `$HOME/.config/opencode` under it:
#
#   mkdir: cannot create directory '/home/blitzlog/.config/opencode':
#   Permission denied
#
# which aborted the entrypoint (set -e) before the agent ever started.
# Mounting a tmpfs at `$HOME/.config` with the agent's own uid/gid
# makes the mountpoint uid-owned, and Docker then mounts the
# `$HOME/.config/gh` bind INSIDE it (parents are mounted before
# children). The bind's own mountpoint stays root-owned, which is
# correct: that one is read-only.
#
# The rule this encodes: ANY mount point under `$HOME` needs its own
# uid-owned tmpfs, because Docker will otherwise create its parent as
# root.
BLITZLOG_TMPFS_MOUNTS="--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,mode=1777 --tmpfs ${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_HOME}:rw,nosuid,nodev,uid=${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_UID},gid=${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_GID},mode=0700 --tmpfs ${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_HOME}/.config:rw,nosuid,nodev,uid=${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_UID},gid=${BLITZLOG_CONTAINER_GID},mode=0700"

# Bind-mounted paths the container may only READ. The GitHub credential
# store and the gh CLI config are owned by the HOST and rewritten there
# by the token-refresh poll loop (issue #145), so the container sees
# them read-only and cannot tamper with the host's copy.
BLITZLOG_READONLY_MOUNTS="/home/blitzlog/.git-credentials.d /home/blitzlog/.config/gh /opt/whisper-stt/models"

# --- Tier 3: the tailnet capability exemption -------------------------
# The ONLY relaxation of --cap-drop=ALL in the whole project.
#
# tailscaled needs CAP_NET_ADMIN to create and configure the WireGuard
# interface and CAP_NET_RAW for `tailscale ping`'s ICMP probes, plus
# the /dev/net/tun character device. It also needs a writable path for
# its state and its control socket.
#
# These flags are applied ONLY when TAILSCALE_AUTH_KEY is set — i.e.
# only on runs that actually enrol in a Tailnet. Every other run gets
# --cap-drop=ALL and nothing else.
#
# The container-side Tailnet join is the ONLY enrolment path: the
# Lambda bootstrap no longer installs or joins Tailscale on the host
# (the old `_install_tailscale_script` is gone), so dropping the
# in-container join would remove the local-LLM-over-Tailnet transport
# outright. See issue #164 for the full decision record.
BLITZLOG_TAILSCALE_FLAGS="--cap-add=NET_ADMIN --cap-add=NET_RAW --device /dev/net/tun"
